{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Take a census of the sons of Kehat.</b> According to what we have brought up in parashat Ki Tissa, that through the giving of the ransom it constitutes for them a lifting of the head, therefore the verse said regarding their number ״כִּי תִשָּׂא״ (Exodus 30:12) — unlike the Levites, who did not give a ransom for their number, concerning whom it said ״פְּקוֹד אֶת בְּנֵי לֵוִי״. If so, why did the verse change its language regarding the Levites themselves and revert to saying <b>נָשֹׂא</b> and not פקוד?" "It would appear that because HaShem gave them an inner service — to carry the Ark and the Table — therefore He ascribed to them the language of lifting of the head, as it were, above Gershon and Merari, so that they would be superior to them. And even though Gershon is the firstborn of Levi, Kehat was chosen by Yah, for from him came forth a light to the world — Moshe and Aharon — and the line of justice, since this branch would carry the Ark of the Torah that Moshe placed, who came forth from Kehat." "And be precise in His saying <b>from among the sons of Levi</b>, for the reason we have stated — because he is in the middle between Gershon and Merari — and to him the term תּוֹךְ (midst) is ascribed."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:01.390742960Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}